Chapter 7

Unified Predictive Framework: Mathematical Specification

We present the integrated pipeline as a formal mathematical specification. No software implementation is described.

Definition 7.1 (Megafire Prediction System). At each assimilation time t_k:

1. Prior ensemble: \{\boldsymbol{\theta}_{k|k-1}^{(i)}\} from the previous posterior via the transition kernel of d\boldsymbol{\theta}=b\,dt+\Sigma\,dW.
2. Update: \boldsymbol{\theta}_{k}^{(i)} = \text{EnSF\_update}(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{k|k-1}^{(i)},\mathbf{y}_k) using the score \nabla_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_k|\boldsymbol{\theta}) = \frac{1}{\sigma^2}J_{\mathcal{G}}^T(\mathbf{y}_k - \mathcal{G}(\boldsymbol{\theta})).
3. Criticality index: For each particle, R_f^{(i)} = \lambda(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{k}^{(i)})/(\mathrm{St}(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{k}^{(i)}) + \mathrm{Pe}^{-1}).
4. Megafire probability: P_{\text{mega}}(t_k) = \frac{1}{N}\sum_{i} \mathbf{1}_{\{R_f^{(i)} > R_f^*\}}.
5. Early‑warning: Compute the empirical Fisher metric \hat{g} = \frac{1}{\sigma^2} \hat{J}^T \hat{J} from the ensemble, and monitor \kappa(\hat{g}).
6. Control decision: If an active fire is present and P_{\text{mega}}(t_k) < 1, solve the CLBF‑constrained optimal control to allocate suppression \mu(x,t). If P_{\text{mega}}(t_k) \to 1, declare uncontainability and shift to evacuation planning.

The consistency of this specification under perfect model and infinite ensemble is stated as:

Conditional Statement 7.2 (Correctness). If all Propositions 3.2, 5.1, 6.1, and Conjecture 5.3 hold, then the above system correctly identifies the megafire boundary and prescribes safe control when R_f < R_f^*.

