Chapter 8

Conclusions and Open Problems

This dissertation has developed a mathematical framework that identifies a critical bifurcation threshold for megafire emergence, encoded in the dimensionless Critical Fire Number R_f. The core contributions are:

· A physically grounded definition of R_f as an energy‑balance ratio.
· A proof that a saddle‑node bifurcation of travelling combustion waves occurs at R_f = R_f^* in one space dimension.
· An information‑geometric early‑warning signal based on the divergence of the Fisher–Rao curvature.
· A proof that safe, bounded suppression is possible in 1D if and only if R_f < R_f^*.
· A conceptual Bayesian data assimilation architecture for real‑time estimation of R_f.

